WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:05.690
Sudan's military rulers and a civilian coalition
have agreed in principle to establish a joint

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:07.270
transitional council.

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:09.519
But the makeup of the council is still undecided.

00:00:09.519 --> 00:00:14.690
Thousands of protesters calling for civilian
rule are continuing their weeks-long demonstration

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:16.500
in the capital Khartoum.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.200
DW's Melanie Cura Daball is there.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:31.080
They call it a sit-in, but here in the streets
of Khartoum nothing is still.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:37.200
Walking among the protestors in the capital
you’re surrounded by transfixing scenes

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:42.990
Speeches and poetry on provisional stages,
the echo of revolutionary songs in the air,

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:51.130
Sudanese flags fluttering everywhere
Jubilation across the generations is the overwhelming

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:57.060
sound you hear all over town - nevertheless,
people here in Sudan keep on insisting their

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:59.480
fight isn’t over just yet.

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:02.760
A lot of the peoples demands have not been
yet.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.680
That’s why we still come here.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:09.100
I have come all the way from El-Gadarif and
I’m going to remain here until the regime

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.970
actually falls.

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.580
Everybody here is united.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:15.720
The people give you a sense of comfort.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:21.210
When you are sitting here there is no fear.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:25.900
These people will only be satisfied when “the
regime steps down completely and power is

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:29.100
handed to a civilian transitional government”.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:36.210
It’s an incredibly well organized and cheerful
protest we are witnessing here: with volunteers

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:41.780
doing security checks, revolutionary art being
created on the streets, and cleaning patrols

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:43.670
taking care of the rubbish.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:49.729
You can tell, these protestors are here to
stay and make sure that their revolution isn’t

00:01:49.729 --> 00:01:54.700
stolen from them.

